.env*.local

# Anything pulled OUT of an env store. `vercel env pull` writes .env.vercel.tmp
# — real credentials, in the repo root, matching none of the rules above. It sat
# untracked and unignored until a `git add -A` swept it into a commit on
# 2026-09-04; GitHub's push protection refused the push, which is the last line
# of defence and not one to rely on.
.env*.tmp
.env.vercel*

# Env backups. `.env*.local` does not match `.env.local.bak-1785633128`, so a
# timestamped copy sat untracked in the repo root until GitHub's secret scanner
# caught it on the way out. Anything derived from an env file is a secret.
.env*.bak*
.env.local.*

# Credentials for the PostgREST contract suite. Never committed.
.env.contract
